Hello!

I tested the memory usage on a Windows machine with 9 hgu133plus2 chips. 
On disk these files took 284 MBs. After reading the data in R, the stored
AffyBatch consumed about 100 MBs of memory. But, during the construction of
an AffyBatch object using the ReadAffy() command, R consumed a maximum of
about 700 MBs. During the normalization, the memory need was much lower,
about 200 MBs.

I'm not sure whether you can extrapolate from these results, but assuming
you can, this would mean that you would need about 7 GBs of memory in order
to be able to load all 88 chips at the same time using ReadAffy().

Best regards,
Jarno



